		{
			dependencies: ["164E55E7C8C64782"]
			description: [
				"The forge is used to heat materials to high temperatures. The time it takes to heat up items is substantially faster than the Pit Kiln, and easier to handle as well."
				""
				"To make a forge, youll need 7 charcoal, and 5 rock-like blocks. Cobblestone, raw stone, and bricks will work."
				""
				"A guide on how to specifically create the forge can be found in the Terrafirmacraft guidebook."
			]
			id: "4DD311059ED9736D"
			tasks: [{
				icon: "minecraft:coal_block"
				id: "31AB1CD99D89C937"
				observe_type: 0
				timer: 0L
				title: "Look at Charcoal Forge"
				to_observe: "tfc:charcoal_forge"
				type: "observation"
			}]
			title: "Forge"
			x: 3.0d
			y: -13.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3F5C75EDC0AF1F64"]
			description: [
				"The Charcoal Pit is a way of obtaining Charcoal. Charcoal pits are made with Log Piles. To place a log pile, Right Click and Shift while holding a Log. More logs can be inserted by either pressing Right Click directly while holding a log, or by pressing Right Click with something else to open the interface."
				""
				"The charcoal pit is formed by surrounding log piles with solid, non-flammable blocks. The amount of charcoal produced is proportional to the amount of logs contained inside the log piles. To start the burning process, light one of the log piles, and then cover it. If it worked, you should see smoke particles rise up from the structure."
				""
				"After the charcoal pit burns out and stops smoking, you will be left with Charcoal piles. The charcoal pile contains up to 8 layers of Charcoal. Dig it with a shovel to obtain the charcoal items. Charcoal piles can be added to or placed with Right Click."
			]
			id: "164E55E7C8C64782"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7EA292229B03519F"
				item: "minecraft:charcoal"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Charcoal Pit"
			x: 0.0d
			y: -13.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"656DE0626BD91E80"
				"4DD311059ED9736D"
			]
			description: ["A Bellows is a device which can be used to increase the air flow through another device which lets them burn at a hotter temperature. However, by burning at a hotter temperature they will also consume fuel faster. The bellows can provide air to a device that is directly in front of it, or in front and one block down. This allows it to provide air to a Firepit, or a Charcoal Forge for example."]
			id: "02D0C6AD820F70EB"
			tasks: [{
				id: "0900F730449FC03F"
				item: "tfc:bellows"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 15.0d
			y: -13.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["656DE0626BD91E80"]
			description: ["A leather flask is a direct upgrade from the Jug as it holds much more water in it."]
